  "tldr": "A finite binary process is observed through a bounded window and a lag-abstracted directed and bidirected summary graph. The paper deliberately admits directed effects only at positive lags through \\(L\\), a restriction suited to delayed actuation or transmission at the sampling resolution; bidirected dependence may span any two summary-compatible time points in the observed \\(H\\)-window and is not bounded by \\(L\\). The sharp controlled-micro-direct-effect envelope is the attained extrema of a finite union of raw semi-Markovian response-function polynomial programs, with exact real-algebraic endpoint and SCM certificates. It collapses to the Ferreira--Assaad adjustment functional, is strictly narrower than graph-free order-only bounds on a relative-open, explicitly defined graph-compatible temporal-instrument family with four rational primal--dual endpoint certificates, and supports simultaneous tie-aware inference. The first-class open question compares a fully defined branchwise quotient-simplex image with the exact push-forward of overlapping independent edge-latent product measures, beginning with a quantified equality-or-separating-witness test on \\(A_0\\leftrightarrow B_0\\leftrightarrow C_0\\) plus \\(A_{-1}\\to C_0\\).",
