  "related_work": "Ferreira and Assaad (2026, Theorem on controlled micro direct effects) provide the summary-graph query setup and the adjustment expression recovered by the collapse theorem, but leave sharp sets outside their sufficient regime untreated. The absence of instantaneous directed arrows and the directed-lag bound \\(L\\) are deliberate restrictions of this paper, not assumptions attributed to Ferreira--Assaad or Jahn--Karnik--Schulman; they model delayed causal transmission, while bidirected lags remain unrestricted within the observed window. Duarte et al. (2024, Propositions 1--2 and Algorithm 2) provide the canonical response-function and polynomialization method adapted within each refinement; the exact real-algebraic layer adds terminating endpoint isolation, causal-size bounds, and decoded SCM witnesses. Jahn, Karnik, and Schulman (2025, Propositions 1--2) show that a known bounded-lag periodic ADMG can be cut to a finite segment for identification; their work informs finite-window reasoning but is not the source of the present positive-directed-lag restriction or a theorem-level extension target. Rossetto and Antonucci (2026, theorem on the reduced linear program and its Appendix proof) motivate the internally defined comparator over all finite response signatures consistent with the strict temporal order; its exact extrema are defined here over the observationally constrained SCM fiber rather than by reference to an external LP. Choe et al. (2026, Proposition 3.1) also quotient a linear program over an unrestricted signature simplex. Their reverse lifts need not lie in the explicitly defined push-forward family \\(\\overline{\\mathcal P}_{G,\\mathcal J}^{\\mathrm{fac}}\\), which retains independent overlapping edge-latent products. Evans (2016, Theorem 4.13 and Proposition 7.4) motivates retaining latent-margin structure beyond displayed ADMG constraints, and Evans (2021, Theorem 6.4) shows how hidden-variable dependence constructions can exploit nonlocal graph structure. Geiger and Meek (1999) and Basu, Pollack, and Roy (1996) supply the exact-elimination and complexity ancestors. Bellot (2024, Propositions 3--5) demonstrates that partial graphical information can improve graph-free bounds but does not give the temporal micro-CDE strictness region. The strictness instance uses \\(H=L=1\\): the independent edge latents \\(A_{-1}\\leftrightarrow X_{-1}\\leftrightarrow Y_0\\) create the sixteen-state binary response program, while the only permitted \\(X\\to Y\\) placement forces the focal arrow \\(X_{-1}\\to Y_0\\); the full rational observational table, response-type endpoint masses, and dual inequalities are part of the formal certificate. Malloy, Tripathy, and Nowak (2020, Theorem 1) motivate whole-multinomial coverage, while Assaad, Ez-Zejjari, and Zan (2023, Proposition 7 and Theorem 1) supply the downstream direct-effect root-cause comparison made uncertainty-aware by the same-SCM tie rule.",
  "technical_internal_limitation": "The exact quotient push-forward \\(\\overline{\\mathcal P}_{G,\\mathcal J}^{\\mathrm{fac}}\\) preserves the raw image by construction, but it does not itself reduce the latent product parameterization. Computational reduction replaces that induced family by branchwise unrestricted quotient-simplex masses, and this replacement may enlarge the image. The mandatory first test fixes \\(H=L=1\\), \\(A_0\\leftrightarrow B_0\\leftrightarrow C_0\\), \\(A_{-1}\\to C_0\\), and the singleton controlled effect of \\(A_{-1}\\) on \\(C_0\\); failure must be recorded by an algebraic quotient point and an exact nonmembership certificate and forces the unquotiented route.",
  "honest_scope": "The paper deliberately excludes instantaneous directed effects and directed lags beyond \\(L\\); it places no \\(L\\)-bound on bidirected lags, which may span the full observed \\(H\\)-window. The envelope is the smallest closed interval containing all attainable CDE values; the attainable set itself is not asserted to be connected. The finite-window model is the target, so no stationarity or infinite-history reduction is assumed. Exact certification is worst-case singly exponential in the number of raw response-weight variables and is intended as a certificate engine, not a claim of polynomial-time scalability. The unquotiented compiler, collapse, strictness, and simultaneous-coverage results are theorem targets. The order-only comparator is the exact envelope of its stated temporal-order SCM fiber, and the strictness neighborhood is relative to the positive laws having a nonempty summary-graph refinement fiber. The edge-latent-chain witness uses \\(H=L=1\\), and contains explicit rational observational, primal, and dual tables for all four endpoints. Equality of the raw and exact factorized push-forward images is a fidelity lemma; equality with the unrestricted quotient-simplex image, a factor-preserving selector, and the quotient-size bound remain open and must first survive the stated six-vertex kill test. When the refinement class is a singleton, the construction reduces to the known fixed-graph response program, and on the Ferreira--Assaad graphical regime it reduces further to their adjustment functional.",
